":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nNot reproducible in Godot v4.6.1.stable -Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21914.8004) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700U with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.32 GiB memory\n\nNot reproducible in Godot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9595) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.86 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\nReproducible in \n\nNot reproducible in Godot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21914.8004) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700U with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.32 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\nReproducible in Godot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21914.8004) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700U with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.32 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21914.8004) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700U with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.32 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot crashes upon loading a project in 4.7 that opened fine on 4.6, but only on one of my computers and only when using Vulkan instead of D3D12.\nUpon opening the project, it is responsive for a while and then either the code screen flashes, a large amount of errors are printed and Godot crashes, or Godot hangs and then crashes.\n\nThe printed errors are:\n\n<img width=\"1149\" height=\"484\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82c2bd2b-dab9-4dc4-a860-800f0a46273d\" />\n\nAnd here's a video of it:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6106e957-221d-454d-97d8-465cc5f19c9c\n\n\nStrangely enough it does not happen on empty projects (or projects with some Godot.svg sprites strewn around).\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHappens a couple seconds after opening the project. Sometimes it prints the error text, sometimes the engine just hangs and nothing happens. Unfortunately does not happen on an empty (or almost empty) project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis happened in two larger projects, and I'm not capable of replicating it in a new one. I hope the specifics and the errors are enough to somewhat pinpoint the error.\nIf you don't care about size, you can find one of them at: https://gitgud.io/madodev/ero-slayers (NSFW) though I've moved that one from vulkan to d3d12 by now so you'll have to switch it back in 'rendering device' to make it crash.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120534/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120534/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}